          "stateDigest": "sha256:cf93ed9be1610caca023d5300f171cfbe2884528d1585ef29bd7d917b6b11fe3",
          "affectedItems": [
            "B",
            "C"
          ],
          "issue": "The owner has to choose the toast wording before I write it, so I'm stopping before the planner, executor and verifier steps. I haven't changed any files.\n\nBoth options name the address. They differ in what the toast says happens next. Option 2 says the mail app is opening, so it would only be accurate if `useCopyEmail.ts` actually opens it on failure. That would be a separate behavior change, and the task doesn't include it.\n\nWhich wording should `copyFallback(address)` return?\n1. `Couldn’t copy. Email me at <address>.`\n2. `Couldn’t copy the address. Opening your mail app to <address>.`",
          "recommendation": null,
          "options": [
            {
              "key": "1",
              "kind": "choice",
              "label": "`Couldn’t copy. Email me at <address>.`"
            },
            {
              "key": "2",
              "kind": "choice",
              "label": "`Couldn’t copy the address. Opening your mail app to <address>.`"
            }
          ],
          "consequences": {
            "1": "item B resumes with this answer",
            "2": "item B resumes with this answer"
          },
